WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.040
There are so many new beauty releases

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:03.180
happening all the time,

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.220
so we gathered some of
the most-hyped products

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:06.690
to test for ourselves.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:08.880
This month, I tested out a lot of products

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.350
from Simihaze Beauty.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:11.580
This is a new brand for me,

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.680
so let's start with the stuff I liked.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.735
The Solar Tint blush duo comes with

00:00:15.735 --> 00:00:17.970
a cheek pigment and a cheek gloss.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.561
These both went on really easily,

00:00:19.561 --> 00:00:21.394
and the pigment is so good.

00:00:21.394 --> 00:00:24.090
Surprisingly, I loved
the cheek gloss more,

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.360
even though it's not super
practical for all-day wear.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.822
I didn't love the color
of this Velvet Blur

00:00:29.822 --> 00:00:31.890
matte lip balm on my skin tone,

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.170
but the formula itself was so good.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:35.700
It has the comfort of a lip balm

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.610
but the pigment and blurring
effect of a matte lipstick.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.920
It's creamy and super comfortable.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:42.450
I thought the Lunar lip gel

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:45.630
and the Super Slick mini
lip balm were just OK.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:46.920
The lip gel was pretty,

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.750
but the formula was nothing special.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.940
It's just a thin lip gloss.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.023
The mini lip balm was pretty moisturizing,

00:00:53.023 --> 00:00:54.330
and the tint is cute,

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:56.790
but it's so little
product for what you pay.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.410
Again, nothing special.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.600
Now for the products I just didn't like.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.540
I wanted to love the Sun
Flush all-over face tint,

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.640
but it just ended up being really patchy

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.770
and broke up my foundation.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:09.523
And I tried this a few different ways

00:01:09.523 --> 00:01:11.490
to see if I was just applying it wrong,

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.890
but it still messed up
my foundation underneath.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.780
The Easy Lash Clean Lift mascara

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.610
just didn't do much for my lashes.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:18.690
I didn't get much lift,

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:20.220
I got little to no volume,

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.200
and my lashes weren't
lengthened very much.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.840
Overall, I love the
packaging of this brand,

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.550
and it does have some standout products,

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:28.380
but I think it's all very overpriced

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.660
for how the actual formulas perform.

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:32.130
Everyone has been raving

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.440
about the Summer Fridays Lip Butter Balms.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.750
This set with the minis
is limited-edition,

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.270
but they sell all of
these shades in full size.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:41.580
I ended up really enjoying these.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.535
The formula is on the thicker side,

00:01:43.535 --> 00:01:44.640
but not sticky.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.260
They feel really moisturizing,

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:49.290
and I like how they give
an almost lip-gloss effect.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:50.850
I loved all of the tinted balms,

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:53.100
but I think Poppy was my favorite.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.590
They all give a pretty,
subtle wash of color,

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:57.330
and they have this nice vanilla scent

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:58.740
that's not overpowering.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:00.180
I'm obsessed with these.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.087
This is the Danessa Myricks Beauty

00:02:02.087 --> 00:02:04.620
Lightwork IV Transcendence palette.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:05.670
I'm not gonna lie,

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:09.090
I was very intimidated
by this palette at first.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:10.980
It has four different formulas:

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.655
velvet chromes, which are
color-shifting powders;

00:02:13.655 --> 00:02:16.491
pressed chrome flakes,
which are flaky toppers;

00:02:16.491 --> 00:02:19.350
glass metallics, which are
super-reflective powders;

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:21.658
and aqua chromes, which
are water-activated

00:02:21.658 --> 00:02:23.250
duo-chrome pigments.

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:25.230
So there is a lot going on.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:27.510
I started applying over a light wash

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:30.270
of black eye-shadow base to
make the colors pop more,

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:32.700
but I don't even think
I needed to do that,

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:35.820
because these powders are so pigmented.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:38.280
I was determined to use all
of the different formulas,

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:41.220
so I added one of the
metallics in the inner corners

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.200
and put the chrome flakes in the center.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.760
The flakes were the only formula

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.380
that was a little difficult to work with,

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:49.200
only because they're kind of
hard to pick up and apply,

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.330
but I think they added
a really cool texture

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.160
and color shift to the eye look.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:54.930
I used an aqua chrome for some eyeliner,

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:57.030
and it's so reflective and sparkly,

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.320
and it dried down quickly.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.167
This palette is extremely pricey,

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:03.030
and I did get some slight fallout,

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.040
but the quality is definitely there,

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.980
and I think it's so much
more versatile than it seems.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:10.230
The shades in here are so transformative

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.540
and really inspire you
to play with your makeup.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.580
Plus, it can also be used on the face.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:16.320
These are the L'Oréal Colour Riche

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:18.240
Intense Volume matte lipsticks.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.830
I thought these were going to be similar

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:22.560
to the Nars Powermatte
lipstick I tried a while ago,

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.120
but the formula is different.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.700
The color payoff on these is so good,

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.530
and they apply really smoothly.

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:31.038
This is one of the most
comfortable matte formulas

00:03:31.038 --> 00:03:33.963
I've ever tried, especially
from the drugstore.

00:03:33.963 --> 00:03:36.270
What makes this lipstick
different from the Nars one

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:39.180
is that it's unfortunately
not transfer-proof.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:41.310
To be fair, it claims to be smudge-proof,

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:42.810
so it's not the same thing.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:44.580
Regardless, I think these lipsticks

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:45.840
are comfortable on the lips,

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:47.460
and the colors are so rich,

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.380
so I really like them.

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:51.930
Apparently Gwen Stefani
has her own beauty brand

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:54.541
called GXVE, and this is
the first product from it

00:03:54.541 --> 00:03:56.040
that I've ever tried.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:59.280
This is the Double Dippin'
2-1 lip color remover

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.930
and hydrating lip mask.

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:03.442
I wanted to test it out with
my Nars Powermatte lipstick,

00:04:03.442 --> 00:04:06.180
since it's one of my
hardest-to-remove lipsticks.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:08.400
The formula of this lip mask feels

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.590
like a makeup-removing cleansing balm.

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:13.470
If you've never tried one,
they feel really oily.

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:14.645
Because of that, it actually

00:04:14.645 --> 00:04:16.290
broke the lipstick down really well.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.240
It made it super easy to remove.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:21.148
However, as a regular
lip mask, it just feels

00:04:21.148 --> 00:04:24.485
way too oily and thin to be comfortable.

00:04:24.485 --> 00:04:26.250
This just feels like one of those products

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:27.675
that they market as multiuse

00:04:27.675 --> 00:04:29.241
to make it sound more innovative.

00:04:29.241 --> 00:04:31.230
Lights Lacquer just released
its winter collection,

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:32.460
called Cocktail Hour.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:34.170
I do own a lot of their polishes,

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:36.000
so this isn't a new brand for me,

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.758
but I definitely think this is my favorite

00:04:37.758 --> 00:04:39.810
color story they've ever done.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:42.090
The polishes have those wide, flat brushes

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.320
I love for applying.

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:45.810
It just makes it so
much easier and faster.

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:46.980
I tried the cream shades,

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:48.690
Old Money and Audrey, first,

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:50.640
and both were full coverage in two coats,

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.040
and the application was really smooth.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.260
Then I tried the jelly
shade, called Lady in Red.

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:56.580
Because this is a jelly,

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:58.170
it's way more sheer than a cream,

00:04:58.170 --> 00:04:59.995
so I ended up doing two thicker coats

00:04:59.995 --> 00:05:01.145
for full color payoff.

00:05:01.145 --> 00:05:03.300
The color is slightly lighter on my nails

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:06.283
than in the bottle, but
still pretty and so shiny.

00:05:06.283 --> 00:05:09.245
Next I tried To the Nines,
which is a metallic polish.

00:05:09.245 --> 00:05:10.890
I really love this color,

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:13.230
but this formula is
probably the least forgiving

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:15.210
when it comes to streaks and bubbles.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.790
My two absolute favorite
shades from the collection

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:20.190
are Whiskey Neat and Diamonds Are Forever.

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:22.320
Whiskey Neat is also a metallic formula,

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:23.970
but it's more of a duo-chrome,

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:26.280
and Diamonds Are Forever
is like a milky taupe

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:28.350
with a bunch of superfine glitter in it.

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:31.080
I don't think these colors
separately are anything new,

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.450
but I love how they all work
together in this collection,

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:35.493
and the formulas are all so good.

